  "live_records": {
    "q-33823": {
      "dom_id": "step-q33823",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨1,1,0⟩+t⟨-1,1,1⟩+s⟨0,2,2⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-1,1,1⟩$ and $w=⟨0,2,2⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =2j-2k \\\\  & =⟨0,2,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨0,2,-2⟩.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
