    "q-70981": {
      "dom_id": "step-q70981",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $H(-3,2,7)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨3,-1,20⟩+s⟨-3,0,1⟩$ and $r=⟨0,3,-4⟩+t⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-3,0,1⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $H(-3,2,7)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $h=⟨-3,2,7⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =h+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨-3,2,7⟩+s⟨-3,0,1⟩+t⟨2,1,-\\frac{1}{5}⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-70981-a",
