<mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo fence=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">⟩</mo><mo>,</mo><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace></mstyle><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></td></tr></tbody></table><div class=\"questionWidget-buttonBar\"><div class=\"questionWidget-submitButton disabledButton\" style=\"display: none;\">Submit</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-spinnerFrame\"><div class=\"questionWidget-spinner\" style=\"display: block;\"></div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-result\"><div class=\"questionWidget-correctIncorrectIcon\"><img src=\"/img/correct-answer.svg\"></div><div class=\"questionWidget-correctText\">Correct</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-explanationHeader\">EXPLANATION</div><div class=\"questionWidget-explanation\"><p>First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"30\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mover><mjx-over style=\"padding-bottom: 0.105em;\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-stretchy-h class=\"mjx-c2192\" style=\"width: 1.592em;\"><mjx-ext><mjx-c></mjx-c></mjx-ext><mjx-end><mjx-c></mjx-c></mjx-end></mjx-stretchy-h></mjx-mo></mjx-over><mjx-base><mjx-mrow><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D437 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D438 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-mrow></mjx-base></mjx-mover></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>D</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> and <mjx-co