    "q-128497": {
      "dom_id": "step-q128497",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨3,\\sqrt{7},-2⟩+t⟨-2,8,0⟩+s⟨3,-1,-1⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-2,8,0⟩$ and $w=⟨3,-1,-1⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-8i-2j-22k \\\\  & =⟨-8,-2,-22⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-8,-2,-22⟩.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
